<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portuguese Restoration War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1640–1668</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Acclamation War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Portuguese Restoration War was fought from 1640 to 1668 after Portugal rebelled against Spanish rule and proclaimed John IV of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-braganza">House of Braganza</a> king, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberian-union">Iberian Union</a>. After long border warfare, Portuguese victories at Ameixial (1663), Castelo Rodrigo (1664) and Montes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claros">Claros</a> (1665) led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> to recognise Portuguese independence in the Treaty of Lisbon (1668).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portuguese-restoration-war.jpg" alt="Portuguese Restoration War" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johannes_der_vierte_K%C3%B6nig_zu_Portugal_und_Algarbe_etc,_ca_1650.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
